  "details": "I would want to be able to change the view of the Desktop View when in VR as using a High FOV headset causes the view to be highly stretched towards the sides. I know its only currently mirroring one eye ( I think its the right eye) so anything on the same side is stretched and the view on desktop is not centered. Would it be possible to set the desktop view to stitch between both eyes at the same time so I would be able to get a more central view without having to use and setup the stream camera option. Images attached show how stretched the view is.",
